# __TITLE__ domain agents

Domain agents built on the rulegraph kernel. Each agent is a planner scoped to one
branch of the taxonomy; its executors are rule-domain investigators. An agent can
answer a question directly, from its domain's point of view, or work on a task
delegated by a core planner and report findings with evidence.

The example knowledge (order decisions: credit, fulfillment, charges) is a
placeholder. Replace it domain by domain, keeping `validate`, `eval` and `pytest` green.

```bash
pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
__DIST__ validate
__DIST__ eval
__DIST__ ask credit ORD-1 "Why was this order rejected?"
pytest
```

| Path | What it is |
|---|---|
| `src/__PACKAGE__/pack/` | Knowledge pack: taxonomy, ontology, field catalog, codes, rule domains, procedures |
| `src/__PACKAGE__/fixtures/` | Sample records and reference data |
| `src/__PACKAGE__/record.py` | Record adapter: status, outcome codes, amounts, dates, derived fields |
| `src/__PACKAGE__/system.py` | Builds the toolbox and domain agents (fixtures or HTTP APIs) |
| `goldens/domain_goldens.yaml` | Questions asked of each domain agent, with expected answers |
